Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: Dolby Vision active area view mode

The "Dolby Vision active area" view mode fits the authored L5 active
area of each picture instead of the whole encoded frame. A 1.43:1 IMAX
master that windowboxes its 2.39:1 scenes then shows those scenes at
full width, and returns to the IMAX frame when L5 changes. The source
rect is cropped only when that enlarges the picture, so frames that
already fit their active area keep the unscaled Master paths. Without
L5, the mode behaves as Normal.

